"Kent Paul Dolan" <xanthian@well.com> wrote 
> "Artemis the Ranger" <wcristalle@hotmail.com> wrote:
> 
> > ... new Quest artifact
> 
> Bottomless can/potion of oil/grease, "+2 to lube"?

I like that. Tik Tok's Oilcan, maybe. Tik Tok (of Oz fame) could even
be the Quest leader. (u)ntrap with it to remove squeaky boards, and
guarantee that a door will not stick. #invoke it to repair rust to
yourself, a rusty item in your inventory, or to recharge an oil lamp.
While carried, it should probably have a couple nice abilities, such
as half magic damage and maybe curse protection a la Magicbane.

I'd suggest that rusting work much like stoning, as mentioned, but
only one stage at a time. Ditto for corrosion. Like wearing a cloak
over armor, armor on an area should probably reduce the chance of
being degraded.

"A gush of water hits your left leg! -<more>-
You rust! -<more>-
Your quickness feels less natural."

So, the first time you get degraded, you lose intrinsic speed (and
cannot regain it while rusted).

"You are splashed by the acid blob's acid! -<more>-
You corrode! -<more>-
You are slowing down."

Then you get slowed. Again, you're stuck with it until you fix
yourself.

"Quaff what?
q - an uncursed potion of water.
You rust further! -<more>-
You die... -<more>-"

And on the third degradation, that's all she wrote.

Repair of course is an issue. Repairing this sort of damage probably
should not remove the speed loss, so this race would probably want
keep a wand of speed monster handy. Blessed potions of acid and
potions of oil would probably be the best bets for repair; it'd
probably be easiest if (q)uaffing them removed the appropriate damage.

Greasing oneself should probably be allowed, as a layer of protection
against rust and acid.

This race should probably have an intrinsic "hard helmet" for falling
rock traps, be immune to mind flayers, be immune to stoning, be immune
to death rays, resist sleep, and have magical breathing. It should
probably have a built-in spellcasting penalty. I'd give it built-in
fumbling, too, to help balance things.

Whatever other classes are available, Ranger should be allowed. Healer
probably shouldn't.

As mentioned, food might be an issue. I like Artemis' idea about lumps
of coal, which could be generated as a percentage of rocks (including
falling rock traps). Perhaps automotons could also eat wands, with the
occasional side effects, and nutrition based on charges. I'd kill off
the hero as soon as it would otherwise faint.

"You run out of power. -<more>-
You die... -<more>-"

Some possible side effects:

Polymorph, Teleportation, Speed Monster, Make Invisible - Chance of
gaining the intrinsic.
Slow Monster - Chance of losing the intrinsic, or becoming slowed.
Cancellation - Chance of a random intrinsic loss (like a gremlin's
special).
Fire - High nutrition value. Chance of gaining fire resistance.
Fireball - Very high nutrition value.
Cold - Low nutrition value. Chance of gaining cold resistance.
Nothing - Zero nutrition value, gain an experience level.
Lightning - Chance of gaining shock resistance.
Wishing - Chance of gaining a random intrinsic.
Secret Door Detection - Chance of gaining automatic searching.
Locking - Lowers dexterity, chance of losing intrinsic speed, or
becoming slowed.
Opening - Like a tripe ration for humans, chance of stunning,
confusion, and "Your furnace flies open!" causing nutrition loss.
Death - Level drain.
Digging - Does damage.
Sleeping - Chance of _losing_ sleep resistance.
Healing - Acts as a potion of healing.

If you add the race to SLASH 'EM, it could have an "idle" #technique.
When used, the automoton would consume no nutrition as long as it
stood there doing nothing.

Anyhoo, just a few random ideas to throw into the mix. 

